CORE libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp17 --stdlib libc++
^\[main\.assertion\.1\].*: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
After the 2026 "template-only no-match silently throws" fix
(resolve: silently discard template-only no-match per [temp.deduct]/8),
the surface symptom changed: std::apply's
`decltype(auto)` tuple-based forwarding path that previously failed
with CONVERSION ERROR is now caught by the enclosing convert_function
catch, leaving an empty main() that verifies vacuously (the
__CPROVER_assert(r == 3, "apply") never makes it into the goto
program).  Expected-when-fixed now requires the main assertion line
to be SUCCESS in the output; until the libc++ tuple deduction path
actually completes, this test stays on the KNOWNBUG list.
Minimal header-free reproducer: cpp11_tuple_leaf_no_body.
Round-11 third batch (2026-08-04): the get redirect now compares
parameter TYPES position-normalized ([dcl.fct]/5, [temp.over.link]/6);
the whole family RUNS BMC end-to-end.  Remaining layer visible as
no-body FAILUREs: std::__1::get<0,...>'s DEFINITION body is not
instantiated for the call (apply_basic reaches VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL
but main is still dropped -- props=0, caught by this desc).
Round-16 (2026-08-06): the get layer is FIXED (multi-pack spec
absorption + lockstep value substitution; CORE
cpp11_tuple_get_return_type_body).  Remaining layer: the tuple
CONSTRUCTOR itself has no body
(tuple(this, rref_signed_int, rref_signed_int) -- the _EnableUTypesCtor
enable-if ctor machinery); get assertions still fail through the
unconstructed object.
Round-19 (2026-08-07): FIXED end-to-end -- the constructor layer fell
in three stages: has_conflict candidate gates ([temp.deduct.type]/2),
multi-pack function templates ([temp.variadic]/5,7,8, the five-pack
__tuple_impl ctor), and multi-pack lockstep in mem-inits and base
specifiers (heterogeneous leaf types).  CORE with non-vacuous
assertions; g++/clang++ replicas verified along the way
(cpp11_multi_pack_ctor, cpp11_tuple_size_alias_spec,
cpp11_member_alias_empty_pack).
